TEXT -448 -224 Left 2 ;Degenerated common emitter / source: the same circuit without the bypass capacitor, so RE/RS stays in the signal path (local series feedback).\nAv = −(RC ∥ RL) / (1/gm + RE). Next to RE = 1k, 1/gm (≈ 18 Ω for the BJT, ≈ 120 Ω for the MOSFET) barely counts: both give about −(RC ∥ RL)/RE ≈ −3.2, that is −3.1 (9.9 dB) and −2.8 (9.0 dB).\nMuch less gain, but it hardly depends on the transistor, it is linear (200 mV in and no visible distortion), the bandwidth is wider and Rin goes up (β·RE for the BJT).\nAt high frequency Cgs (55 pF) ties the MOSFET's source to its gate and its gain climbs a little before rolling off.
TEXT -256 -64 Left 2 ;BJT: BC547C
TEXT 576 -64 Left 2 ;MOSFET: 2N7000
